From 9f1dc3c4a809274c11da5180d018eac4e1fd40e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:25:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] hw/arm/filogic: rename hw/arm/mt7981 (MediaTek Filogic
 family)

The emulation started with the MT7981 and grew to the MT7986, MT7987
and MT7988, which share their peripherals.  Name it after the family:

  hw/arm/mt7981/           -> hw/arm/filogic/
  mt7981.h                 -> filogic.h
  mt7981_router.c          -> filogic_router.c  (the four machines)
  mt7981_leds.[ch]         -> filogic_leds.[ch]
  mt7981_{eth,pinctrl,spim,sysctl,toprgu,msdc,wmac}.c
                           -> mtk_*.c  (MediaTek IP blocks)
  mt7987_pcie.c            -> mtk_pcie.c
  mt7981_dramc_tbl.h       -> mtk_dramc_tbl.h
  CONFIG_MT7981            -> CONFIG_MTK_FILOGIC

QOM types, state structs and functions follow (mtk-eth / MtkEthState /
mtk_eth_*, ...).  The machine names (mt79xx-router), the MT7981 address
and IRQ constants and the flash file prefix stay.  No functional change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015RfXBtBMqiJKuedv8fLHqT
